<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Macregol Gospels</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 800</span> · Also known as Rushworth Gospels</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Macregol <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gospels">Gospels</a>, or Book of MacRegol, is an illuminated Irish gospel book of about 800, written by Mac Regol, abbot of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/birr">Birr</a>, who died in 822. Decorated in the Insular style with evangelist portraits and elaborate initials, it was later glossed in Old English and is now in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bodleian-library">Bodleian Library</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxford">Oxford</a>.</p></div>
